{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 69, :comments ["<b>According to their power</b> — He speaks in reference to the congregation, for the heads of the fathers gave only two thousand darics of gold and two thousand two hundred of silver, for so it is explicitly stated in the second count. And when he says six thousand in one total, he means to say, between the congregation and the heads of the fathers and the rest of those who volunteered from the kingdom of Cyrus." "<b>Darics</b> — gold dinars." "<b>Thousands</b> — the alef replaces the doubling, and likewise: בזאו נהרים (rivers of gold)." "<b>Minas</b> — weights, and its fellow, the mina, and the Targum: seven minas equals seven shekels."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {3 "The syntax of 'וחבירו המנה יהיה' is obscure; translated hyper-literally. Possibly corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:41:51.731541268Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}